  "body": "Campbell 14th ed., Ch.3 [[p.321-323]] + revision of whole chapter. **Concepts = meri taraf se. Numbers = book se, page ke saath.**\n\n## 1. Post-op management [[p.321-323]]\n\n- No universal protocol. **Pre-op teaching session** helps\n- Posture: ~**15 deg abduction**; posterior approach: triangular pillow (loose straps, **peroneal nerve**); DAA: ordinary pillow\n- Day 0: ankle pumps, quadriceps and gluteal isometrics, gentle rotation, gait training. **Straight leg raise NOT helpful after THA** (groin pain, rotational stress on stem)\n- Weight bearing: **cemented = tolerance**; cementless ingrowth = 6-8 wks limited by some, others early (Hol: no harm; but protect on stairs: torsional loads); structural graft / revision: crutches ~**3 months**\n- Discharge when: bed transfers, level walking, few steps\n- **Hip precautions questioned:** meta-analysis (1122 pts), unrestricted patients more satisfied, return faster, **no increase in dislocation**\n- Self-directed PT: about 1/3 needed formal PT (Klement)\n- First 6 weeks: elevated toilet seat, pillow between knees, showers not baths. Drive at **2-4 wks**\n- Abductor weakness persists to **1 year** (Foucher)\n- Work: sedentary 4 wks; limited lifting 2-3 months; **no manual labour**\n- **OK:** swimming, cycling, golf. **Avoid:** jogging, racquet sports (impact)\n- Follow-up: **2 wks, 6 wks, 3 months, 1 year**, then periodic. Routine X-ray **every 2 years** (loosening, wear, osteolysis can be asymptomatic)\n\n## 2. Eight tough concepts\n\n> [!samajh] **Offset**\n> Offset badhane se abductor ka lever lamba, load kam, impingement kam. Length badhaye bina offset badhana ho to medial neck attachment / high-offset stem.\n\n> [!samajh] **Cup position**\n> Inclination 40 +/- 10, anteversion 15 +/- 10 sirf starting point. **Stiff spine = zyada anteversion + inclination. Flatback/hypermobile = kam.** Cup + stem combined anteversion ~35 (25-50).\n\n> [!samajh] **Dislocation direction**\n> Anterior = cup ya stem zyada anteverted. Posterior = retroverted ya capsule/rotators repair nahi. Posterior repair se dislocation 4.46% se 0.4%.\n\n> [!samajh] **Stress shielding**\n> Stem diameter^4 stiffness. Bada, CoCr, extensively coated = zyada proximal bone loss. Revision me bone stock ka problem.\n\n> [!samajh] **Femur Dorr and stems**\n> A (champagne flute) cemented/cementless dono. C (stovepipe, old women) = cemented ya careful. > 75 yrs registry me cemented better.\n\n> [!samajh] **PJI decision**\n> Early / acute haematogenous + stable = DAIR + liner/head change. Chronic ya loose = implant out, two-stage (3 months). Sinus, unknown/virulent organism = two-stage.\n\n> [!samajh] **Acetabular defects**\n> Cavitary = graft + oversize cup. Segmental large = augment ya structural graft (>= 50% host support). Discontinuity = plate/distraction/cup-cage/triflange.\n\n> [!samajh] **Femoral defects (Paprosky)**\n> Isthmus > 4 cm = extensively coated/fluted. < 4 cm = impaction grafting / fluted tapered. Nothing = composite / megaprosthesis.\n\n## 3. Key numbers\n\n| Topic | Number | Page |\n|---|---|---|\n| Abductor lever ratio | ~2.5:1 (arthritic 4:1) | 179-180 |\n| Joint force: stance / lifting-running | 2.6-3 x BW / up to 10 x BW | 180 |\n| Stress shielding stem size | >= 13.5 mm | 181 |\n| Head >= 36 mm dislocation | 0.05% | 185 |\n| Cement mantle | 4 mm proximal, 2 mm distal | 187-188 |\n| Pore size | 100-400 µm | 188 |\n| Dual mobility dislocation | 0.9% primary, 1.3% revision | 195, 262 |\n| HXLPE wear / threshold | 0.003 / 0.1 mm/yr | 197 |\n| Ceramic head fracture | delta 1:100,000; alumina 1:5000 | 199 |\n| Asymptomatic bacteriuria | not a contraindication | 200 |\n| Sacral slope normal / stiff | 11-30 / <= 10 deg | 204 |\n| Safe cup (Lewinnek) | 40 ± 10 incl, 15 ± 10 anteversion | 260 |\n| Cement injection / stem insertion (Simplex) | ~4 min / ~6 min | 220 |\n| Cup target | incl 40-45, anteversion ~20, combined 25-40 | 210-212 |\n| Crowe I-IV | < 50, 50-75, 75-100, > 100% | 235 |\n| DDH lengthening limit | 3-4 cm | 235 |\n| Loosening if cup in false acetabulum | 2-3 x higher | 236 |\n| Neck fracture: fixation vs arthroplasty failure | 43% vs 6% | 242 |\n| Dislocation fall with anterior approach | 8% to 2% | 244 |\n| Fusion conversion failure at 10 yrs | 33% (Mayo) | 249 |\n| HO: radiation / NSAID | 500 cGy / 6 wks (7 d works) | 254 |\n| PE rate (modern) | 0.21% | 254 |\n| Prophylaxis duration | 10-14 days to 35 days | 255 |\n| Nerve palsy: OA / DDH / revision | 0.5 / 2.3 / 3.5% | 255 |\n| Vascular injury | 0.04% primary, 0.2% revision | 256 |\n| Superior gluteal safe zone | 5 cm above trochanter | 256 |\n| Shuck test | 2-4 mm | 258 |\n| Dislocation primary / revision | ~3% / 9.04% | 259 |\n| Trochanteric nonunion dislocation | 17.6% vs 2.8% | 262 |\n| Intra-op femur fracture primary / revision | 1.7% / 12% (cementless 3% / 19%) | 263-264 |\n| Trochanteric nonunion | 3-8% primary, 9-13% revision | 268 |\n| PJI rate | 1-2% | 270 |\n| ICM 2018 score | >= 6 infected, 3-5 inconclusive, < 3 not | 274 |\n| ESR / CRP chronic | > 30 / > 10 mg/L | 273 |\n| Two-stage 90-day mortality | 2.6% | 276 |\n| Aspiration: antibiotics off | >= 2 weeks | 273 |\n| Cup loose: lucency | >= 2 mm in 3 zones (94% loose) | 280 |\n| Gruen / DeLee zones | 7 / 3 | 278 |\n| Barrack cement grades | A white-out, B <50%, C 50-99%, D complete | 278 |\n| Narkbunnam score loosening | >= 5 | 283 |\n| Alpha-defensin false positive in ALTR | 31% | 285 |\n| ETO union | 98-99% | 292 |\n| Cortical perforation with burr | 10% | 298 |\n| Paprosky femur isthmus | 4 cm | 312 |\n| Impaction grafting survival | 98.8% aseptic at 20 yrs | 317 |\n\n> [!verify] Exam se pehle important numbers ek baar book mein khud match kar lena.\n\n## 4. Not covered here\n\n> [!flag] **Ch.4 Surface Replacement (resurfacing)** aur **Ch.5 Hip Arthrodesis** is app me abhi nahi daale. Chahiye to bol dena.\n"
